  <static seed="1238" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicAlgebra/LinearEquationApplications/MXPlusBWordProblem40.pg">
    <statement><p>Peter hired a face-painter for a birthday party. The painter charged a flat fee of <m>{\$50}</m>, and then charged <m>{\$4.50}</m> per person. 
In the end, Peter paid a total of <m>{\$176}</m>. How many people used the face-painter<rsq/>s service?</p>
<p><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/> people used the face-painter<rsq/>s service.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>28</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>Let <m>x</m> be the number of people who used the face-painter<rsq/>s service.</p>
<p>The charge for each person was <m>{\$4.50}</m>, so the charge for <m>x</m> people was <m>4.5x</m> dollars. There was also a flat fee of <m>{\$50}</m>.</p>
<p>Now we can write an equation:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 4.5x+50 = 176 }</m></p>
<p>Next, we solve for <m>x</m>:</p>
<p><m>\begin{aligned}
  4.5x +50 \amp = 176 \\
  4.5x +50\mathbf{{} -50} \amp = 176\mathbf{{} -50} \\
  4.5x      \amp = 126 \\
  \frac{4.5x}{4.5} \amp = \frac{126}{4.5} \\
  x   \amp = 28
\end{aligned}</m></p>
<p>So twenty-eight people used the face-painter<rsq/>s service.</p>
</solution>
